WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Your French penfriend writes: «J'habite
ici depuis trois ans.» Word for word:

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.780
I live here since three years.

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.240
Is that a mistake?

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.090
English would say: I have been
living here for three years.

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.270
A longer, heavier tense.

6
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.940
Then she adds: «Je viens
de manger.» Word for word,

7
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.850
I come from eating.

8
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.710
But she hasn't gone anywhere.

9
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.230
So why does French say I
live here since three years,

10
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.170
when English says I have been living here?

11
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.650
In this mission, you'll
learn to ask how long

12
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.700
someone has been doing something.

13
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.910
Then you'll place sentences
on a timeline in the lab:

14
00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.160
past, now, and ahead.

15
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: find out what
French time phrases really say.
